      "title": "Pages and Records: Storage Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Pages and Records: Storage Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pages and Records",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Page== = fixed-size disk block, the smallest unit the DB reads or writes",
                "Often 4-16 KB: {blue:8 KB} PostgreSQL, {purple:16 KB} InnoDB",
                "One row lookup reads the ==whole page==",
                "Record lives in a ==slot==; slot directory maps slot number to byte offset",
                "Record ID = ==(page number, slot number)=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Record ID",
                    "sub": "(page 7, slot 2)",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Page 7",
                    "sub": "one disk read",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Slot directory",
                    "sub": "slot 2 → offset",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Record",
                    "sub": "bytes at offset",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Heap Files and Record Layout",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Heap file== = pages in no particular order",
                "No index means a ==full scan== of every page"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Fixed-length",
                "Variable-length (VARCHAR)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Find field",
                  "simple offset calculation",
                  "needs the **slot directory**"
                ],
                [
                  "Too big?",
                  "no",
                  "can {red:overflow} into extra pages"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cost Model",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Speed is measured in ==page I/Os==, not rows",
                "Fewer pages touched = ==faster query==",
                "Heap scan of 1,000 pages = 1,000 I/Os, even for one row"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Count pages, not rows",
              "text": "A 1-row lookup still costs a **whole page** read. Without an index, it costs every page."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Primary vs Secondary and Clustered vs Non-Clustered",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Primary vs Secondary and Clustered vs Non-Clustered",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Primary vs Secondary",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Primary index}: built on the ==primary key==, unique and not null",
                "{blue:Secondary index}: built on **any other column**, can be non-unique"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Clustered vs Non-Clustered",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Clustered",
                "Non-clustered"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Leaf holds",
                  "the **full row**, in key order",
                  "key + **pointer** to the row"
                ],
                [
                  "Pointer",
                  "none, row is in the leaf",
                  "heap: record ID; InnoDB: ==primary key=="
                ],
                [
                  "Per table",
                  "==only one==",
                  "many"
                ],
                [
                  "Range scan",
                  "adjacent pages, sequential",
                  "random row fetches"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Secondary index",
                    "sub": "find the key",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Primary key",
                    "sub": "read from leaf",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Clustered index",
                    "sub": "second traversal",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Row",
                    "sub": "found",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Range Scans",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Clustered range: read ==adjacent pages== in order",
                "Non-clustered range: one ==random fetch== per matching row"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "InnoDB secondary lookup",
              "text": "It costs ==two traversals==: secondary index to get the primary key, then the clustered index to get the row."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "B+ Trees: The Default Index Structure",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "B+ Trees: The Default Index Structure",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Shape of a B+ Tree",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Internal nodes hold ==keys + child pointers== only",
                "{green:Leaves} hold all the data or row pointers",
                "Leaves form a ==doubly linked list==: find start key, walk sideways for a range",
                "Node = one page, fan-out in the ==hundreds==: millions of rows, only 3-4 levels"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lookup Cost and Splits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lookup = ==O(log_f N)== page reads, f = fan-out",
                "3 levels = **3 page I/Os**, root usually cached"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Insert into a full leaf",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Leaf full",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Split in two",
                    "note": "two half-full leaves",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Push separator up",
                    "note": "parent gains a key",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cascade to root",
                    "note": "tree stays balanced",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Composite Index (a,b,c)",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX idx_abc ON t (a, b, c);"
              ],
              "note": "leftmost-prefix rule"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Filter",
                "Uses idx_abc?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`a`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a` + `b`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`a` + `b` + `c`",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`b` alone",
                  "{red:no}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Leftmost prefix",
              "text": "Skip `a` and the index cannot help. Put the column you always filter on **first**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Hash Indexes vs B+ Trees",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Hash Indexes vs B+ Trees",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Hash Index",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Hash function== on the key picks a **bucket**",
                "Equality `WHERE id = 5`: ==O(1) average==",
                "{red:No range, ORDER BY or prefix}: hashing destroys key order",
                "Collisions: **chaining** in bucket or **overflow pages**",
                "Too many collisions: lookups slide toward ==O(n)=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Hash vs B+ Tree",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Hash",
                "B+ tree"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`=`",
                  "O(1), faster",
                  "O(log N)"
                ],
                [
                  "`<` `>` BETWEEN",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "ORDER BY",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`LIKE 'abc%'`",
                  "{red:no}",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. In Practice",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "CREATE INDEX idx_id ON t USING hash (id);"
              ],
              "note": "PostgreSQL"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "MySQL ==InnoDB==: **adaptive hash index**, built automatically in memory",
                "PostgreSQL: `USING hash`; **B+ tree is the default** in both"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why can't a hash index do BETWEEN?** Hashing destroys key order, so neighbours are not adjacent",
                "**When pick hash over B+ tree?** Equality-only lookups; it is faster for `=`",
                "**Why can a hash index slow down?** Heavy collisions push lookups toward O(n)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Equality only: hash. Range or sort: ==B+ tree==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Index Maintenance Cost, Mistakes and Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Index Maintenance Cost, Mistakes and Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a write costs",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Statement",
                "Table",
                "Indexes touched"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "INSERT / DELETE",
                  "written",
                  "{red:every index}"
                ],
                [
                  "UPDATE indexed column",
                  "written",
                  "that index: entry ==moves=="
                ],
                [
                  "UPDATE unindexed column",
                  "written",
                  "{green:none}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**5 indexes** = about ==6 structures== written per row"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Index on ==every column==: slower writes, wasted memory and disk, planner may pick wrong",
                "==Low cardinality== (boolean, gender): planner prefers a full scan anyway",
                "==UUIDv4== clustered key: random inserts cause page splits and fragmentation",
                "Sequential keys just ==append== to the last page"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Index only what you use",
              "text": "Columns in ==WHERE==, ==JOIN== and ==ORDER BY== only."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cheat sheet",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Pick"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Equality only",
                  "{purple:hash}"
                ],
                [
                  "Range or sort",
                  "{blue:B+ tree}"
                ],
                [
                  "Clustered index",
                  "one per table"
                ],
                [
                  "Composite index",
                  "leftmost prefix"
                ],
                [
                  "Read-heavy table",
                  "more indexes"
                ],
                [
                  "Write-heavy table",
                  "fewer indexes"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
